			<item>
				<title>Complete Beginner&#39;s Guide: How to Install Git and Push Code to GitHub</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/my-website/posts/github-guide/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/my-website/posts/github-guide/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;This guide covers the steps required to start pushing your code to Github.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;step-1-download-and-install-git&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Step 1: Download and Install Git&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#step-1-download-and-install-git&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Before running any Git commands, you will need Git installed on your computer.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;windows&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Windows&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#windows&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Download the installer from &lt;a href=&#34;https://git-scm.com/downloads&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;git-scm.com&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;&lt;img src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/my-website/posts/github-guide/download_git.png&#34; alt=&#34;Alt text&#34;&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Run the &lt;code&gt;.exe&lt;/code&gt; file and accept the default settings during setup.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Open &lt;strong&gt;Command Prompt&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;Git Bash&lt;/strong&gt; to verify the installation:&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;git --version&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;linux-ubuntudebian&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Linux (Ubuntu/Debian)&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#linux-ubuntudebian&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Simply open your terminal: &lt;strong&gt;Ctrl+alt+t&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Grassy Dreams</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/my-website/posts/grassy-dreams/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/my-website/posts/grassy-dreams/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;So, for a while now, I&amp;rsquo;ve been really interested in grass. :)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/my-website/posts/grassy-dreams/grass.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;grass&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;note all puns are intended&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Like, I even wonder what cows must think when they see some green, juicy grassland. They&amp;rsquo;d probably be like, &amp;ldquo;Woah, woah, Tabby, come check this out!&amp;rdquo; And Tabby would be like, &amp;ldquo;Come on, bet you&amp;rsquo;ve never been to the Meadow of Pinks.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Yeah, so for a while now I&amp;rsquo;ve been playing Far Cry 3. This is kinda my first time though, and I really took an interest in the visuals&amp;hellip;.especially the grass. It really caught my eye&amp;hellip; or eyes, maybe. Something about the lush fullness of it all.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Cube mappy, Another reinvention of the wheel</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/my-website/posts/cubemappy/</link>
				<pubDate>Wed, 17 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/my-website/posts/cubemappy/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;As you may know, I have a knack for reinventing things that already exist. Most of the time, though, it&amp;rsquo;s for learning purposes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;One example is Cube Mappy, a project I started to sharpen my Python skills, and improve my Defold experience.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;At its core, Cube Mappy is a simple tool that converts 360° panoramic images into six separate images, each representing one face of a cubemap, exactly what Defold likes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
